     "title": "2.1 Physical problem",
     "html": "<p>The geometry is a finite-width flat plate with a central through-wall crack of total length 2c. The plate thickness is t and the plate half-width is W. The crack is assessed using Mode I opening stress intensity. Primary stresses control both fracture and plastic collapse. Secondary and residual stresses contribute to crack-tip driving force and are treated separately in the FAD interaction procedure.</p>",
     "text": "The geometry is a finite-width flat plate with a central through-wall crack of total length 2c. The plate thickness is t and the plate half-width is W. The crack is assessed using Mode I opening stress intensity. Primary stresses control both fracture and plastic collapse. Secondary and residual stresses contribute to crack-tip driving force and are treated separately in the FAD interaction procedure."
