     "title": "2.3 Why KIP and KISR are kept separate",
     "html": "<p>Primary loading is required for equilibrium and contributes to both KIP and reference stress. Secondary and residual stresses are not treated as additional primary collapse load. Their contribution is included through KISR and the Phi/xi interaction treatment. This distinction is fundamental to the implemented Level 2 assessment.</p>",
